WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.820
Take two cuttings from one hydrangea bush.

2
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.700
Plant them in two gardens.

3
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.040
When they bloom, one can be blue and the other pink.

4
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.160
The two cuttings have the same genes.

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.800
So where does the difference come from?

6
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.160
Are all my traits from my genes, or do some come from how I live?

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:26.983
Some traits are inherited.

8
00:00:27.843 --> 00:00:31.803
An inherited trait is passed from parents to offspring through genes.

9
00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:35.943
Eye color is one. Other traits are acquired.

10
00:00:36.823 --> 00:00:41.223
An acquired trait is a characteristic a living thing gets during its life.

11
00:00:42.043 --> 00:00:46.523
A scar is one. So are dyed hair, and muscles built by exercise.

12
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.337
Why can't a scar be passed on?

13
00:00:51.237 --> 00:00:53.557
A new animal grows from sex cells.

14
00:00:54.517 --> 00:00:56.517
Sex cells carry the parent's genes.

15
00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.457
A scar changes skin cells.

16
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:02.337
Lifting weights changes muscle cells.

17
00:01:03.257 --> 00:01:05.597
Neither changes the genes in the sex cells.

18
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:07.797
So neither reaches the offspring.

19
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.150
Genes are not the whole story.

20
00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:15.930
The environment is everything around a living thing that can affect it.

21
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.810
Soil, light, water, food and temperature are all part of it.

22
00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:25.910
Many traits depend on genes and the environment together.

23
00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:28.403
Back to the hydrangea.

24
00:01:29.003 --> 00:01:34.083
In many bigleaf hydrangeas, acidic soil lets the roots take up more aluminum.

25
00:01:34.823 --> 00:01:36.903
The aluminum helps make the flowers blue.

26
00:01:37.643 --> 00:01:39.863
In less acidic soil, the flowers are pink.

27
00:01:41.003 --> 00:01:42.863
Gardeners measure this with soil pH.

28
00:01:43.563 --> 00:01:45.983
A lower number means more acidic soil.

29
00:01:46.643 --> 00:01:49.223
About 5.0 to 5.5 gives blue.

30
00:01:49.823 --> 00:01:51.783
In between, the color is in between.

31
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:55.443
Above about 6.0 to 6.5 gives pink.

32
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:58.937
So, are all my traits from my genes?

33
00:01:59.777 --> 00:02:05.097
No. In many hydrangeas, the genes set which colors are possible.

34
00:02:05.757 --> 00:02:08.157
The soil helps decide which one appears.

35
00:02:09.137 --> 00:02:10.617
Your height works this way too.

36
00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:15.457
It depends on many genes, and on food and health while you grow.

37
00:02:16.777 --> 00:02:19.077
Traits coded in genes can be inherited.

38
00:02:19.077 --> 00:02:24.617
A scar, dyed hair or a learned skill cannot be passed to offspring.
